{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00700 - MONDO_grouped_1200_1134_15512_5080_100078",
  "verbalization": "Eplerenone is associated with Hypertension through a series of indirect pathways, all of which involve the treatment of Hypertensive Disorder. The evidence suggests that Eplerenone is used to manage Hypertensive Disorder, which in turn is linked to Hypertension. This relationship is supported by the shared indication of Hypertensive Disorder across multiple pathways, indicating a common therapeutic target. The presence of multiple drugs (Mibefradil, Hydralazine, and Methyldopa) that are also linked to Hypertension further reinforces the notion that Hypertensive Disorder is a central node in the network of hypertension management. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Hypertensive Disorder as a mediator in the relationship between Eplerenone and Hypertension, suggesting a potential mechanism involving the regulation of blood pressure through the modulation of vascular tone or renin-angiotensin systems. The evidence does not provide direct evidence of Eplerenone's mechanism of action on blood pressure, but the indirect pathways suggest a plausible link through the treatment of Hypertensive Disorder.",
